{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 11, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Raymond Berengar and the Count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was a Crusader and a prominent figure in the Kingdom of Jerusalem during the 12th century.\n\n**Early Life**\n\nRaymond III was born in 1143 to Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. His family was of noble origin and had significant influence in the region. Raymond III's early life is not well documented but it is known that he was educated in the court of Baldwin III King of Jerusalem.\n\n**Marriage and Succession**\n\nIn 1160 Raymond III married Humberga of Thiers he was married for only a few months before she died. He then married Eschiva of Bures in 1160. They had no children but adopted a son named Bohemond III Prince of Antioch. Raymond III's marriage to Eschiva was likely a strategic move to secure his position as Count of Tripoli.\n\n* **Key Events of his Reign** *\nIn 1174 Raymond III was forced to recognize the authority of the Kingdom of Jerusalem after the death of the Count of Tripoli. However in 1175 he was able to secure recognition as the Count of Tripoli from the Kingdom of Jerusalem. In 1184 Raymond III was a member of the delegation that met with Saladin the Sultan of Egypt and Syria.\n\n**Later Life and Death**\n\nIn 1186 Raymond III was one of the leaders of the Crusader army that was defeated by Saladin at the Battle of Hattin. He was taken prisoner and held captive by Saladin until his death in 1187. His death marked the end of the House of Raymond Berengar as the Counts of Tripoli.\n\n**Legacy**\n\nRaymond III's legacy is complex and multifaceted. He was a prominent figure in the Kingdom of Jerusalem and played a significant role in the Crusades. However his reign was also marked by conflict and power struggles. Despite his complex legacy Raymond III remains an important figure in the history of the Crusades and the Kingdom of Jerusalem.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.021772763}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00021634146}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0012805604}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.12215032}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.8980677e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00026020003}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -2.396078e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.02390643}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.27687913}, {"token": " member", "logprob": -0.6368367}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -2.467602e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0058953688}, {"token": " House", "logprob": -0.24102856}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -5.6146e-05}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -2.245768}, {"token": " Ber", "logprob": -1.8157874}, {"token": "eng", "logprob": -0.33865476}, {"token": "ar", "logprob": -0.32383245}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.5168052}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.6175496}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -1.2739196}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.00029702543}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0021453716}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -0.00044383688}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.19915111}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.021614}, {"token": "115", "logprob": -0.012796314}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -0.0009470269}, {"token": " until", "logprob": -0.2376943}, {"token": " his", "logprob": -0.089863785}, {"token": " death", "logprob": -0.004791445}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.18479025}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.0012896087}, {"token": "118", "logprob": -0.00025638632}, {"token": "7", "logprob": -0.0016693241}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.032118034}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.15893151}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.06839073}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.8373836}, {"token": " Crus", "logprob": -2.3248377}, {"token": "ader", "logprob": -2.4079987e-05}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.44829452}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.83668905}, {"token": " prominent", "logprob": -1.6165295}, {"token